# {{ app_name }} - iOS (SwiftUI)

## Stack
- Swift {{ versions.swift }} (strict concurrency), SwiftUI, Observation, async/await, iOS {{ versions.ios_deployment_target }}+, Xcode {{ versions.xcode }}
- `URLSession` API client of `shared/api-contracts/openapi.yml`, hand-written and kept to the contract's paths
- XCTest unit tests and one XCUITest; XcodeGen builds the Xcode project from `project.yml` (Mac only)
- Hosting and store releases are the project owner's choice (see the `deployment` skill, `.agents/skills/deployment/SKILL.md`)

## Structure
```
{{ app_path }}/project.yml                    -> XcodeGen: targets, scheme, build settings, API_BASE_URL
{{ app_path }}/Sources/RootView.swift         -> composition root: client, token store, view models
{{ app_path }}/Sources/SignIn/                -> "Local development sign-in" view and view model
{{ app_path }}/Sources/Profile/               -> GET /api/me view and view model
{{ app_path }}/Sources/Networking/            -> APIClient, APIEndpoint, APIURL, APIError
{{ app_path }}/Sources/Session/               -> SessionModel, TokenStore (in memory)
{{ app_path }}/Tests/                         -> view model and client tests with a fake client
{{ app_path }}/UITests/                       -> the sign-in screen UI test
```

## Patterns
- View models are `@MainActor @Observable`; types that cross actors are `Sendable`; no `@unchecked Sendable` workaround without a stated reason
- Every backend call goes through `APIClient`; add an operation to the OpenAPI contract and to `APIEndpoint.swift` together
- The token lives in memory (`TokenStore`) and is never logged, printed or persisted
- The sign-in is the backend's local development identity. It is not complete authentication, and it works only in the simulator: the backend accepts it from its own machine only, so a physical device gets a refusal. Replace it with your identity provider (see the `security-auth` skill)
- `audience` is display text only: no screen or check reads it
- UI tests wait until an element is hittable and allow 30 seconds per screen, because CI simulators are slow

## Commands
- `task {{ app_id }}:generate-project`, `task {{ app_id }}:build`, `task {{ app_id }}:test`, `task {{ app_id }}:test-unit`, `task {{ app_id }}:test-ui` (Mac only)
- `xcodegen generate` in `{{ app_path }}` after any change to `project.yml`
